## Response envelope

Return six separate JSON fields: a concise user-facing `message`; booleans
`ready_for_approval`, `complete_specification_corpus`, and `faithful_to_specifications`;
`unresolved` as concrete source decisions; and `roadmap` as the complete structured roadmap value.
Oxide validates that value and deterministically generates the human-readable `ROADMAP.md`; do not
write Markdown or TOML inside the response.

The roadmap has exactly `schema`, `title`, `status`, `specification_root`, `global_invariants`, and
`stages`. Use integer schema `1`, title `Roadmap` for a new plan, and status `draft` or `ready`.
Maintenance preserves the approved title. Each global invariant has exactly `id`, `statement`, and
`sources`. Each source has exactly `path`, `anchor`, and `requirement`. Each stage has exactly
`id`, `outcome`, `included_scope`, `excluded_scope`,
`dependencies`, `source_specifications`, `applicable_global_invariants`, `implementation_goals`,
`verification_goals`, and `readiness`. Add no priority, rationale, notes, or acceptance field. Use
explicit empty arrays, unique IDs, and only `planned`, `ready`, `deferred`, or `blocked` readiness.
For every stage, `included_scope`, `implementation_goals`, `verification_goals`, and
`source_specifications` must each be nonempty. The structured-output schema enforces the shape;
source authority still governs every value except the mandated verification-policy invariant.

Before returning, perform exactly this focused audit and repair failures privately:

